{"id": "gsm8k_train_05091", "action": "R", "latency_ms": 10186.633172212169, "raw_answer": "To determine how many cans of frosting Paul will need, we'll calculate the amount of frosting required for each type of item and then sum them up.\n\n### Step-by-step Breakdown:\n\n1. **Layer Cakes**:  \n   - Paul uses **1 can of frosting per layer cake**.  \n   - He needs **3 layer cakes**.  \n   - Frosting needed: $ 3 \\times 1 = 3 $ cans.\n\n2. **Dozen Cupcakes**:  \n   - Paul uses **1 can of frosting per dozen cupcakes**.  \n   - He needs **6 dozen cupcakes**.  \n   - Frosting needed: $ 6 \\times 1 = 6 $ cans.\n\n3. **Single Cakes**:  \n   - Paul uses **½ can of frosting per single cake**.  \n   - He needs **12 single cakes**.  \n   - Frosting needed: $ 12 \\times \\frac{1}{2} = 6 $ cans.\n\n4. **Pans of Brownies**:  \n   - Paul uses **½ can of frosting per pan of brownies**.  \n   - He needs **18 pans of brownies**.  \n   - Frosting needed: $ 18 \\times \\frac{1}{2} = 9 $ cans.\n\n### Total Frosting Needed:\n$$\n3 \\text{ (layer cakes)} + 6 \\text{ (cupcakes)} + 6 \\text{ (single cakes)} + 9 \\text{ (brownies)} = 24", "generated_token_ids": [1249, 8253, 1246, 1657, 42632, 315, 98181, 6898, 686, 1184, 11, 582, 3278, 11047, 279, 3311, 315, 98181, 2567, 369, 1817, 943, 315, 1509, 323, 1221, 2629, 1105, 705, 382, 14374, 14822, 14319, 29208, 15623, 2923, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 9188, 356, 2050, 95518, 2303, 256, 481, 6898, 5711, 3070, 16, 646, 315, 98181, 817, 6193, 19145, 334, 13, 2303, 256, 481, 1260, 3880, 3070, 18, 6193, 47569, 334, 13, 2303, 256, 481, 41220, 287, 4362, 25, 400, 220, 18, 1124, 15136, 220, 16, 284, 220, 18, 400, 42632, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 5404, 5679, 10861, 61992, 95518, 2303, 256, 481, 6898, 5711, 3070, 16, 646, 315, 98181, 817, 20403, 87893, 334, 13, 2303, 256, 481, 1260, 3880, 3070, 21, 20403, 87893, 334, 13, 2303, 256, 481, 41220, 287, 4362, 25, 400, 220, 21, 1124, 15136, 220, 16, 284, 220, 21, 400, 42632, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 10888, 356, 2050, 95518, 2303, 2